---
import captures from "../data/captures.json";
---

<section class="privacy-section section">
  <div class="wrap privacy-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">05 / LOCAL BY PRINCIPLE</p><h2>
        Your configuration<br />is not our business.
      </h2><p>
        ConfigLens analyses files on your machine. It does not send
        configuration anywhere, run a client, or execute the things it finds.
      </p><ul class="privacy-list">
        <li>
          Configuration is read-only. Snapshot and explicit report outputs are
          intentional writes; diff reads the supplied reports.
        </li><li>
          Share mode reduces identifying details. Redaction is not a guarantee
          of anonymity — review before sharing.
        </li><li>
          Unix snapshots use owner-only permissions. Windows snapshots inherit
          the destination folder’s ACL; use a private directory.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div><div class="redaction-panel">
      <div class="inspector-title">
        <h3>Protection, made visible.</h3><span class="tiny-label"
          >SYNTHETIC ONLY</span
        >
      </div><label class="check-label"
        ><input type="checkbox" id="show-projection" checked /> Show CLI redaction
        projection</label
      ><p class="small muted">
        Captured for <code>{captures.commands.redaction.pointer}</code>. The
        input below is a deliberately fake demonstration value.
      </p><pre
        id="redaction-output">{JSON.stringify(captures.commands.redaction.projection,null,2)}</pre><p
        class="redaction-warning"
      >
        Protected values compare as <code>unknown_redacted</code>, not
        “unchanged”.
      </p><a
        class="text-link"
        href="https://github.com/ob4cl/configlens/blob/main/README.md#privacy-and-caveats"
        >Read the privacy boundaries ↗</a
      >
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
